    {
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus"},
      "description": "Per-second rate of Task exception events over a 15m window: parked (any parkReason - the successor to the old give-up counter, and since v2.0.0 the ONLY counter of a failure) and agent-pod TTL expiry broken out by handoff (agent, synthetic, none - contract G.7, the successor to the old handover counter). Broken out by handoff and NOT by outcome: outcome answers how the POD was stopped (graceful|force_deleted) and says nothing about whether continuation state survived, which is the only thing an exceptions panel wants. handoff=none is the work-loss bucket (tatara-operator#527, shipped in tatara-operator#569). tatara_lifecycle_idle_stop_total and tatara_lifecycle_implement_empty_retry_total have no successor metric in the task-centric redesign (contract K.1) and are dropped rather than mapped onto something that isn't equivalent.",
