    {
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus"},
      "description": "Terminal Task outcomes (operator_task_terminal_total) broken down by kind, state and stateReason. Under tatara-operator v2.0.0 the terminal set is EXACTLY done|rejected - `failed` and `parked` are gone, because a failure now parks instead of terminating - so the failure axis lives on operator_task_parked_total{parkReason} in the exception-rate panel, not here. stateReason is the disjoint terminal vocabulary: 6 reject reasons (declined, false-positive, tracked-elsewhere, issue-closed, mr-closed-externally, mr-taken-over) plus 2 done reasons (doc-timeout, mr-merged-externally); most deliveries carry no reason at all. Cumulative counts since the operator last restarted. Distinct from the token-cost operator_task_terminal_tokens_total series on the Task Delivery dashboard.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
